  In my latest attempt to ascend a barbarian, Thrud was around 9th level when
on DL14 I found both an altar and a shop.  So, with my scroll of teleportation 
and my ring of invisibility, I robbed the shop.  Poof - instant keystone kops.
Take their worthless corpses and offer them to Crom.  Wow - there's jubilex!
Put 'er there, pal!  Wash tentacle slime off of hand, find another Kop, and
kill him.  Pretty soon the whole daemonic pantheon is wandering around the
dungeon, and they're all *my* friends.  I was feeling pretty special.  But, 
when I was clearing off the altar (throwing the rubber hoses, cream pies, and
other sundry gear around) looks like ol' demogorgon got in the way of that 
rubber hose...he got angry, and SMASH -- Thrud the barbarian is now Thrud the
Compost heap. Sigh.

Question: If you have a ring of conflict and were to try this out, would it be
possible to get the wand of death from Orcus?  He never appeared (and I was 
getting milquetoast like bone devils) so does the game not allow him to be
summoned via human sacrifice?


